-- title:
--   Admissible small constants for a valuation ring above q
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $q \ge 5$, let $M'$ be a nonzero natural number with $q \nmid M'$, and let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` such that the image of $q$ in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ is a nonunit of $A$ (this is the predicate `A.LiesOverPrime q`). Then there exist an intermediate field $k_0$ of $\mathbb Q \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q}$ and an element $\pi_0 \in k_0$ whose image lies in $A$ such that, writing $A_0 := A \cap k_0$ for the pullback of $A$ along $k_0 \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb Q}$: $A_0$ is a discrete valuation ring; its maximal ideal is the principal ideal generated by $\pi_0$; $A_0$ is a henselian local ring; the residue field of $A_0$ is algebraically closed; and every $a \in A$ can be written as $a = c + m$ with $c \in k_0$ lying in $A$ and $m$ in the maximal ideal of $A$. Moreover there exist a prime $\ell$ with $3 \le \ell$, $\ell \ne q$ and $\ell \nmid M'$; an element $\zeta_0 \in k_0$ which is a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$; and an element $\varpi_t \in k_0$ lying in $A$ together with a unit $u$ of $A$ such that $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1} = q\,u$ in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$.
--
--   This packages the arithmetic input — a henselian discrete valuation subring with algebraically closed residue field, cut out inside $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ by an intermediate field, carrying an auxiliary prime $\ell$, a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity and a $(q^2-1)$-st root of $q$ up to a unit — required to descend constructions at $q$ to a small field of definition. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_supersingularRegularProlongation_smoothPointCharts`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_supersingularRegularProlongation_smoothPointCharts) in the supersingular-point analysis of modular curves at the prime $q$.
-- source:
